    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Salvadoran national Kilmar Abrego Garcia has arrived in Madrid, Spain, after voluntarily leaving the United States, following a legal dispute over his deportation to El Salvador in March 2025.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-25:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "A federal judge ordered him to leave the US by November 24, 2026, and he self-deported to Spain by that deadline, avoiding deportation to Africa.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388143927:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "According to the Wikipedia article, Kilmar Armando Ábrego García was illegally deported to El Salvador on March 15, 2025, by the U.S. government, which called it \"an administrative error\".",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388143927:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The map shows Madrid, Spain, the location where reports place him.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-25:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The story is reported by AFP via RFI and Reuters.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-25:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined the story: \"Kilmar Ábrego García arrives in Spain, ending Trump deportation battle\".",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:6b93b27b01b3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined it: \"Kilmar Abrego Garcia self-deports to Spain after lengthy US legal battle\".",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:dbd05e9113fe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined it: \"Kilmar Ábrego García, target of Trump's immigration crackdown, lands in Spain after 'leaving happy'\".",
